   sig="This is the volume that gave the Victorian age its central myths: the enclosed lady, the palace of art and the island of the lotos-eaters became permanent figures for the artist's relation to the world, and the 1832 text's 'obscurity' became the test case for the Victorian debate about difficulty in poetry.",
   alt=["Poems (1832)", "Poems, 1833"],
