   desc="Published in 1847 (revised 1850, 1851, 1853, with the intercalated songs added in 1850), a serio-comic poem on the higher education of women: a prince disguises himself as a maid to enter a women's college founded by the princess he is betrothed to.",
   plot="Prince Gama's son, betrothed in childhood to the Princess Ida, enters her college in disguise with his friends; discovered, he is wounded, nursed, and the college collapses when Ida's heart is touched by the story of a mother's love; the poem ends with the prince's vision of a reconciled relation between the sexes and with the lyric 'Now sleeps the crimson petal'.",
